# =============================================================================
# ¶ — the format operator does not chain
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `value ¶ "spec"` is one format tier; the result is `string` and is not
#     itself a format subject.
#   • A second `¶` in the same expression has no reading, so it is a parse error.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • re-formatting a formatted value in one expression; format the value once,
#     or bind the first result and format that (PARSE030)
#
# See also: scriptum, textus, instans
# =============================================================================

# This exemplum intentionally fails to compile: the second `¶` has no reading.
main {
    let int n ← 255
    print n ¶ "x" ¶ "b"
}
